# The One — environment example
#
# Copy to `.env` (same folder) and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not,
# so never put a real secret here.

# ── Authentication ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two mutually exclusive modes. The API refuses to boot with neither.

# MODE A · Microsoft Entra ID (what production uses).
# Create an app registration at entra.microsoft.com → App registrations → New.
# Who gets in: anyone on AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS enrols themselves on first sign-in
# as AUTH_AUTO_ENROL_ROLE (change their role afterwards in Admin › Users);
# anyone else needs a user row created from Admin › Users first (an invitation).
#ENTRA_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match a "Web" redirect URI on the app registration, character for character.
#ENTRA_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/api/auth/callback
# Comma-separated email domains that may sign in without an invitation
# (default byblosvista.com; "none" = strictly invite-only).
#AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=byblosvista.com
# Role code a self-enrolled account starts with (default om_probation).
#AUTH_AUTO_ENROL_ROLE=om_probation

# MODE B · Local development bypass.
# Pick any seeded user from a list, no password, no Microsoft. The API REFUSES
# TO START if this is true while NODE_ENV=production.
AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true

# ── Public demo (DEMO_MODE) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The ONE sanctioned way to run MODE B on a server: a deliberately public demo
# on SEED DATA ONLY, every real integration off. Two guards keep that promise
# (W4-11):
#  · The API REFUSES TO START while DEMO_MODE=true if any real credential is
#    set beside it — ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET, ECOTRAK_CLIENT_SECRET,
#    CLICKUP_API_TOKEN, QUO_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN,
#    GMAIL_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON, GMAIL_PRIVATE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY,
#    MAIL_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET, SHAREPOINT_CLIENT_SECRET,
#    ESCALATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET, QUO_WEBHOOK_SECRET, SALES_TAX_API_KEY — the 14
#    in DEMO_MODE_SECRET_VARS (config.ts). The message names the one to
#    remove. CRON_SECRET is not one of them: it lets Vercel's cron call our
#    own routes and reaches nothing outside The One — and a demo's cron routes
#    answer 403 before they look at it, so give a demo project its own value
#    or none, never production's. DATABASE_URL is not checked either — its
#    password rides inside the URL and nothing marks it as a credential — so
#    this guard cannot tell a demo database from a real one. The second one
#    can:
#  · Sign-in is refused (403 DEMO_NOT_SEEDED) until the seed has written its
#    marker row (app_meta.seeded, migration 0082) — a database that was never
#    seeded admits nobody, and a real one pointed at by mistake was never
#    seeded. Run `npm run setup` against the demo database — its host is not
#    localhost, so also set ALLOW_SEED=<its host>/<database> (see Database
#    below) or the seed refuses to TRUNCATE it.
# Never set it locally: AUTH_DEV_BYPASS alone is local development.
#DEMO_MODE=true

# Hours a session cookie stays valid.
SESSION_TTL_HOURS=12

# Where the browser lives. Used to redirect back after the Entra round trip, and
# to decide whether the session cookie gets the Secure flag (https → yes).
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ── Ecotrak transitions (rules 2.6.3 / 2.7) ─────────────────────────────────
# What a status change does when the current Ecotrak status would not allow the
# transition it implies. warn (default): the move goes through and the audit row
# says Ecotrak would refuse it. block: the move is refused with a 409. Nothing
# is written to Ecotrak in either mode.
#ECOTRAK_TRANSITION_MODE=warn

# ── Email escalations webhook (rule 7.3.2) ──────────────────────────────────
# The shared secret the external email tool presents on
# POST /api/webhooks/email-escalation (header x-webhook-secret, or
# Authorization: Bearer). Unset = the receiver refuses every call (403) — the
# door exists but is bolted until a key is cut. Generate one with
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# and give the same value to the email tool. Never commit a real one.
#ESCALATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Planned maintenance cron (0051) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel's cron (vercel.json) calls GET /api/webhooks/planned-maintenance-run
# once a day with Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>; the route raises every
# work order that is due. Unset = the cron gets 403; opening the Planned
# Maintenance page and its Raise now button still raise what is due.
#CRON_SECRET=

# ── Calls through Quo + AI quote drafts (0054) ──────────────────────────────
# Quo › Settings › Webhooks: point a webhook at https://<site>/api/webhooks/quo
# for call.completed, call.transcript.completed and call.summary.completed on
# the dispatch lines, and paste its signing key here. Unset = the receiver
# answers 403; calls can still be placed and a transcript pasted by hand.
#QUO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Sign-off sheets (0070): the blank sheet is texted to the technician from a
# Quo line and the signed copy comes back on the same webhook — add
# message.received to the webhook above. QUO_API_KEY is an API key from Quo ›
# Settings › API (workspace owner / admin; A2P 10DLC must be approved for the
# line), QUO_FROM_NUMBER the sending line (E.164 or its PN… id). Unset =
# Share opens the Quo app on the dispatcher's PC with the text pre-filled.
#QUO_API_KEY=
#QUO_FROM_NUMBER=+14695011510
#QUO_API_BASE=https://api.quo.com/v1
# The Claude API key that drafts a quote from a call transcript. Unset = the
# draft page says AI drafting is not configured. QUOTE_AI_MODEL overrides the
# model (default claude-haiku-4-5, the cheapest).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#QUOTE_AI_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# ── The assistant (0068) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above. Unset = the panel says it is not switched on.
# ASSISTANT_DAILY_LIMIT is questions per person per day; 0 switches asking off.
#ASSISTANT_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
#ASSISTANT_AI_EFFORT=medium
#ASSISTANT_DAILY_LIMIT=100

# ── SharePoint folders (0071) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A folder per client and per work order in the team's SharePoint library,
# and approved files copied in. The site, library and the three switches are
# set in Admin › Settings; only the credentials live here. The app
# registration needs an APPLICATION permission on the site — Sites.Selected
# (granted on that one site) or Files.ReadWrite.All — with admin consent.
# Unset = falls back to MAIL_GRAPH_*, then to the ENTRA_* sign-in
# registration; with none of them the Settings card says "credentials not
# set" and nothing is filed.
#SHAREPOINT_TENANT_ID=
#SHAREPOINT_CLIENT_ID=
#SHAREPOINT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Client update emails (0055) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every client update is sent FROM one address. Pick a provider:
#   gmail  = Gmail as MAIL_FROM (the team mailbox is on Google Workspace).
#            A Google Cloud service account whose client id is allowed, in the
#            Workspace admin console (Security › API controls › Domain-wide
#            delegation), the scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send.
#            Paste its downloaded key file whole into GMAIL_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON.
#   graph  = Microsoft Graph sendMail as MAIL_FROM. The app registration needs
#            the Mail.Send APPLICATION permission (admin consent); credentials
#            fall back to the ENTRA_* sign-in registration above.
#   resend = the Resend API; the MAIL_FROM domain must be verified there.
# Unset = Gmail when its key is set, else Resend when RESEND_API_KEY is, else
# no email (the Send button says so). The same cron (hourly, vercel.json)
# sends scheduled updates.
#MAIL_PROVIDER=gmail
#GMAIL_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
#MAIL_FROM=contact@seamlessfm.com
#MAIL_FROM_NAME=Seamless FM
#MAIL_REPLY_TO=
#MAIL_GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
#MAIL_GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
#MAIL_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=
#RESEND_API_KEY=

# ── ClickUp (0078) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A personal API token (pk_…) that can WRITE to the Incoming WOs List. Set it
# in Vercel, never here: this file is committed. Nothing is sent until the
# ClickUp switch in Admin › Integrations is on.
#CLICKUP_API_TOKEN=

# ── Sales tax by ZIP (0076) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The quote builder derives a ZIP's combined rate from its cache table, else
# from a RapidAPI "sales tax by ZIP" API when BOTH are set (the key is sent as
# x-rapidapi-key, the host as x-rapidapi-host), else from a per-state fallback
# table. Unset = cache and fallback only; the % can always be overridden on
# the quote. A real key must never sit beside DEMO_MODE (see above).
#SALES_TAX_API_KEY=
#SALES_TAX_API_HOST=

# ── Servers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
API_PORT=5174
API_HOST=127.0.0.1
WEB_PORT=5173

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node-postgres (pg.Pool) on Postgres 16: locally the server on localhost:5432
# (a native install, or docker-compose.yml under Docker), on Vercel the Neon
# URL. Unset = the local default below. The API and the worker read it here;
# npm run setup does not load this file and takes it from the shell.
#DATABASE_URL=postgres://theone:theone@localhost:5432/theone
# migrate (npm run db:migrate) prefers this when set: Neon's DIRECT host, which
# `neon env pull` / the Vercel integration write beside DATABASE_URL. The
# runner refuses a `-pooler` DATABASE_URL otherwise — a session advisory lock
# is not honoured through PgBouncer transaction pooling. The API keeps using
# DATABASE_URL (W3-6).
#DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
# The seed (npm run setup / db:seed) TRUNCATEs the data tables. It refuses a
# host that is not localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1 unless this spells the
# <host>/<database> of DATABASE_URL — the host as pg opens it (case does not
# matter), the database exactly — type out what you are about to empty
# (W3-14). The refusal prints the exact value to set. The database name alone
# is not accepted: every Neon branch's database is called neondb, so a name
# persisted once would confirm every branch. Put it on the command line, never
# in a profile.
#ALLOW_SEED=<host>/<database>
# migrate: confirms a remote DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED set without DATABASE_URL
# (the refusal prints the exact value). Command line only, never a profile.
#ALLOW_MIGRATE=<host>/<database>
# migrate refuses an already-applied migration file whose checksum changed
# unless this is set; it then accepts and records the new checksums (W3-6).
#MIGRATE_ALLOW_CHECKSUM_MISMATCH=1
